<b><font size=4>PLANTING CONTINUES . . .
WEATHER IMPROVES 
</font></b>
<p>
<b>Denny Dawes</b><br>
<i>Wildlife Habitat Institute (WHI)</i>
<p>
Kurt Dostal, WHI Restoration Manager completed auguring holes for willow cuttings with the mini track excavator on July 1st.  The majority of remaining willow cuttings was planted the next day.  On July 3rd, Kurt staked out the three exclosures planned for the 1997 construction area (Phase II) and placed the final willow cuttings in their appropriate locations within the exclosure sites. Denny delivered materials for the exclosures and Kurt and Sean Towley, WHI Technician, handled the construction. 
<p>
Kurt and Sean also set up the irrigation pipe and pumps, preparing for warm, dry weather ahead. 
<p>
During the third week in July, Kurt and Sean planted 7,500 herbaceous species (10 cubic inch plugs). This season's total plantings of woody and herbaceous species are summarized below:
